  abstract = {Autoregressive video diffusion models produced by distillation frameworks still use a fixed number of denoising steps per frame, wasting computation on predictable frames and under-refining challenging ones. DSA is a confidence-guided adaptive computation framework that introduces a lightweight confidence head, trained jointly with the generator under a distribution-matching distillation objective, to estimate per-frame denoising reliability. At inference, the confidence signal dynamically adjusts the number of diffusion steps: simple frames terminate early for speed, while complex frames receive additional refinement. DSA reaches 22.63 FPS with sub-second latency on H100 GPUs while maintaining competitive VBench quality.},
